1c:["$","div",null,{"children":["$","$L2a",null,{"className":"max-w-[64ch]","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-9","children":[["$","div","01",{"data-reveal":true,"className":"","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-2.5","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"flex h-6 w-6 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-brand font-display text-[0.6875rem] font-bold tabular-nums text-white","children":1}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-sans text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.14em] uppercase text-brand","children":"Local progress"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-3.5 font-display text-[clamp(1.125rem,1.7vw,1.35rem)] leading-[1.65] font-semibold text-ink text-pretty","children":["The development of zakat management and philanthropy over the past two decades has shown ",["$","span","1",{"className":"font-semibold text-ink","children":"significant progress at the local level"}],". Many countries, including Indonesia, have successfully built zakat collection and distribution systems that are more structured, transparent, and directly impactful for society. Various economic empowerment, education, and social service programs based on zakat have yielded tangible results in ",["$","span","3",{"className":"font-semibold text-ink","children":"increasing the income of mustahik"}]," (zakat recipients) and strengthening social resilience at the community level."]}]]}],["$","div","02",{"data-reveal":true,"className":"border-t border-ink/12 pt-8 sm:pt-9","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-2.5","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"flex h-6 w-6 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-brand font-display text-[0.6875rem] font-bold tabular-nums text-white","children":2}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-sans text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.14em] uppercase text-brand","children":"A global challenge"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-3.5 font-sans text-[1.03rem] leading-[1.75] text-body text-pretty","children":["However, this impact is still dominated by local and national approaches, while the challenges faced by humanity are becoming ",["$","span","1",{"className":"font-semibold text-ink","children":"increasingly global"}],". Transnational poverty, humanitarian crises, conflicts, disasters, and the impacts of climate change cannot be resolved in isolation by individual nations. In this context, zakat and philanthropy hold immense potential to serve as ",["$","span","3",{"className":"font-semibold text-ink","children":"instruments of global solidarity"}]," capable of bridging gaps and collectively responding to humanitarian issues."]}]]}],["$","div","03",{"data-reveal":true,"className":"border-t border-ink/12 pt-8 sm:pt-9","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-2.5","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"flex h-6 w-6 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-brand font-display text-[0.6875rem] font-bold tabular-nums text-white","children":3}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-sans text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.14em] uppercase text-brand","children":"Why this theme"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-3.5 font-sans text-[1.03rem] leading-[1.75] text-body text-pretty","children":["The theme “From Local Impact to Global Solidarity: The Future of Zakat and Philanthropy” is chosen to emphasize the need to transform the role of zakat and philanthropy from locally impactful instruments into ",["$","span","1",{"className":"font-semibold text-ink","children":"a collaborative force on a global scale"}],". This transformation demands the integration of management innovation, robust governance, and the alignment of humanitarian values across countries. Without a framework for global solidarity, the impact of zakat and philanthropy will remain fragmented and suboptimal in addressing shared challenges."]}]]}],"$L2b"]}]}]}]
1d:["$","div",null,{"id":"objectives","className":"scroll-mt-[var(--header-h)]","children":["$","$L2c",null,{"title":"Objectives of the 10th ICONZ","intro":"Formulated to address the need to strengthen the role of zakat and philanthropy within an increasingly complex and interconnected global context.","objectives":[{"n":"01","text":"To serve as an international forum discussing the transformation of zakat and philanthropy's role from local impact toward global solidarity in responding to transnational poverty, inequality, and humanitarian crises."},{"n":"02","text":"To encourage knowledge exchange through the dissemination of the latest research findings, case studies, and proven impactful zakat and philanthropy management practices from various countries."},{"n":"03","text":"To strengthen global collaboration among zakat institutions, philanthropic organizations, academics, governments, and related sectors in building an interconnected and sustainable zakat and philanthropy ecosystem."},{"n":"04","text":"To identify strategic challenges, barriers, and opportunities in zakat and philanthropy management to expand social impact from the community level to a global scale."},{"n":"05","text":"To formulate policy recommendations and strategic frameworks for policymakers and zakat managers to enhance the effectiveness of zakat and philanthropy in supporting human development and collective welfare."},{"n":"06","text":"To stimulate scientific work and strategic publications that enrich global literature on zakat and philanthropy, while reinforcing the positioning of zakat as an international social development instrument."}],"labels":{"label":"Objective","of":"of","prev":"Previous objective","next":"Next objective"}}]}]
